                    "message": "Not the biggest fan of the empty loop but it does reduce indentation and makes things a bit more readable"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 148,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I did try to look for an existing function in\nhttps://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/header/algorithm.html\n\nsince mixing the conditional and side effect also does not look super great to me.\n\nBut i couldn't find one which does what i want here (running a function until it returns false).\n\nAlternatively we could pass `std::ranges::subrange<std::string::const_iterator>` and check that for not-empty then erase in the loop body.\n\nAnother way would be to define a 3rd function `fixpoint` to run a function until it returns false but then we have 3 functions :/"
                }
